'''Yinhawangka''' (Inawangga) is a [[Pama–Nyungan languages|Pama–Nyungan language]] of [[Western Australia]]. Dench (1995) believed there was insufficient data to enable it to be confidently classified, but Bowern & Koch (2004) include it among the [[Ngayarda languages]] without proviso.<ref>Bowern & Koch (2004) ''Australian Languages: Classification and the Comparative Method''</ref>

